.TH POLEPLEX 1 "May 2026" "PolePlex v1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
poleplex \- minimalist AUR helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B poleplex
\fI\,command\/\fR [\fI\,options\/\fR] [\fI\,package\/\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
PolePlex downloads, builds, and installs packages from the Arch User Repository (AUR).
It uses regex-based PKGBUILD parsing (no source execution) and optional clean chroot
builds via devtools. Search is interactive when run from a terminal.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBs\fR, \fBsearch\fR \fI\,term\/\fR
Search AUR (interactive TUI in terminal, plain text if piped).
.TP
\fBi\fR, \fBinfo\fR \fI\,package\/\fR
Show detailed package info from the AUR.
.TP
\fBd\fR, \fBdownload\fR \fI\,package\/\fR...
Download PKGBUILD(s) from the AUR (default when no command given).
.TP
\fBinstall\fR \fI\,package\/\fR...
Download + resolve dependencies + build + install (full AUR helper mode).
.TP
\fBb\fR, \fBbuild\fR \fI\,package\/\fR...
Download + resolve dependencies + build only (no install).
.TP
\fBr\fR, \fBremove\fR \fI\,package\/\fR...
Remove previously downloaded packages from the local cache.
.TP
\fBu\fR, \fBupdate\fR [\fI\,dir\/\fR]
Update all downloaded packages in \fI\,dir\/\fR (default: ~/.cache/poleplex/build/).
.TP
\fBh\fR, \fBhelp\fR
Display help message.
.TP
\fBV\fR, \fBversion\fR
Display version information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose debug output.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress color and info.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-path\fR \fI\,dir\/\fR
Working directory for downloads/builds.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tarball\fR
Use tarball instead of git clone.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-chroot\fR
Enable clean chroot builds (requires devtools).
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI\,n\/\fR
Parallel build jobs (default: nproc).
.SH DEPENDENCY RESOLUTION
PolePlex parses PKGBUILD files using regular expressions only — the PKGBUILD
is never sourced or executed. Dependencies are resolved recursively with cycle
detection. Official repo deps are installed via pacman \-\-asdeps. AUR deps are
built leaf-first (dependencies before dependents).
.SH CLEAN CHROOT
When \fB\-c\fR is given and devtools is installed, builds run inside a clean
chroot via mkarchroot + makechrootpkg. A local pacman repository at
/var/lib/poleplex/repo/ is used to chain AUR dependency packages between
builds, ensuring each build sees its prebuilt deps.
.SH PARALLEL BUILDS
AUR dependencies at the same DAG depth are built in parallel (up to \fB\-j\fR
jobs). The local repo is thread-safe via flock.
.SH INTERACTIVE SEARCH
When run from a terminal, \fBpoleplex s\fR opens a full-screen TUI:
.IP \[bu]
Arrow keys / Page Up/Down to navigate
.IP \[bu]
Type to filter results in real time
.IP \[bu]
Enter to install the selected package
.IP \[bu]
q to quit
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from
.IR ~/.config/poleplex/poleplex.conf
if it exists. Variables: BUILD_DIR, CLONE_MODE, CHROOT_ENABLED, PARALLEL_JOBS.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0  Success.
1  General error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Search interactively:
poleplex s firefox
.TP
View package info:
poleplex i spotify
.TP
Download a package:
poleplex d firefox-developer
.TP
Full install with deps:
poleplex install yay
.TP
Build only (no install):
poleplex b yay
.TP
Build in clean chroot:
poleplex \-c install yay
.TP
Remove downloaded package:
poleplex r yay
.TP
Update all:
poleplex u
